hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15932","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, he said, my father informed us, from Ziyad ibn Mina, from Abu Sa'd ibn Abi Fadala al-Ansari, who was of the Companions, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic gathers the first and the last for a Day about which there is no doubt, a caller will call: Whoever associated anyone in a deed he did for Allah the Blessed and Exalted, let him seek his reward from other than Allah the Mighty and Majestic, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic is the most free of partners from shirk."
